---DNS records are resource records that define how systems and services should behave when handling requests for a domain name. For example, when you add `A` records to your domain name's DNS records, you're informing other systems (such as your users' web browsers) to contact those IPv4 addresses to retrieve resources relevant to your domain name (such as your Hosting site files).
---@class gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecord
---@field type? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordTypeEnum|string Output only. The record's type, which determines what data the record contains.
---@field domainName? string Output only. The domain name the record pertains to, e.g. `foo.bar.com.`.
---@field rdata? string Output only. The data of the record. The meaning of the value depends on record type: - A and AAAA: IP addresses for the domain name. - CNAME: Another domain to check for records. - TXT: Arbitrary text strings associated with the domain name. Hosting uses TXT records to determine which Firebase projects have permission to act on the domain name's behalf. - CAA: The record's flags, tag, and value, e.g. `0 issue "pki.goog"`.
---@field requiredAction? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordRequiredActionEnum|string Output only. An enum that indicates the a required action for this record.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordList gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecord[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordRequiredActionEnum "NONE"|"ADD"|"REMOVE"

---A set of DNS records relevant to the setup and maintenance of a custom domain in Firebase Hosting.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordSet
---@field domainName? string Output only. The domain name the record set pertains to.
---@field records? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordList Output only. Records on the domain.
---@field checkError? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.Status Output only. An error Hosting services encountered when querying your domain name's DNS records. Note: Hosting ignores `NXDOMAIN` errors, as those generally just mean that a domain name hasn't been set up yet.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordSetList gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordSet[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"A"|"CNAME"|"TXT"|"AAAA"|"CAA"

---A set of DNS record updates that you should make to allow Hosting to serve secure content in response to requests against your domain name. These updates present the current state of your domain name's DNS records when Hosting last queried them, and the desired set of records that Hosting needs to see before your custom domain can be fully active.
---@class gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsUpdates
---@field discovered? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordSetList The set of DNS records Hosting discovered when inspecting a domain.
---@field desired? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DnsRecordSetList The set of DNS records Hosting needs to serve secure content on the domain.
---@field checkTime? string The last time Hosting checked your custom domain's DNS records.

