---@field maxVersions? string The number of FINALIZED versions that will be held for a site before automatic deletion. When a new version is deployed, content for versions in storage in excess of this number will be deleted, and will no longer be billed for storage usage. Oldest versions will be deleted first; sites are created with an unlimited number of max_versions by default.
---@field cloudLoggingEnabled? boolean Whether or not web requests made by site visitors are logged via Cloud Logging.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.SiteList gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.Site[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.SiteTypeEnum "TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"DEFAULT_SITE"|"USER_SITE"

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.Status
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field details? gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---@alias gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.StatusList gcp.unstable.firebasehosting_v1beta1.Status[]

